Now the onion in the pan is soft.
I remember the video's instructions.
The chef says, 'First put a little turmeric powder.'
So I add turmeric powder into the pan.
Then the chef says, 'After that, add the soft poha there.'
I place the water-soaked poha in the pan.
The chef says, 'Now mix everything well.'
He says again, 'Then cover the pan.'
I mix everything, then I cover the pan.
It steams for two minutes.
After that, I remove the cover of the pan.
The entire dish is a beautiful yellow colour.
Now only the final task is left.
I sprinkle fresh green coriander on top of it.
Then I add the juice of one lemon there.
The aroma of the dish is very good.
The Maharashtrian dish called Kande Pohe is ready.
Now I am waiting for Neha and Amit.
